  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nA lathe section that posted `G96` now cancels it at its end: a bare `G97` right after the main spindle stop (`M05` / `M5`), before any after-operation word (`M01`, `M00`, home). Every following section opens under constant rpm unless it states `G96` itself, and no program ends in constant-surface-speed mode. Both lathe posts take the rule: `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps` and `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`. No other shipped post writes `G96` (`git grep -n G96 assets/posts`).\r\n\r\n### Reproduction (Fanuc lathe, test-bench mill-turn, CSS turning then a `LiveTool` section at 3000 rpm)\r\n\r\nBefore (main at 6a10c5ad):\r\n```\r\nG50 S6000\r\nG96 S200 M03\r\n...\r\nM9\r\nM05\r\nG54\r\n(T0202 EM)\r\nT0202\r\nG98\r\nM1001\r\nM1003 S3000\r\n```\r\nAfter:\r\n```\r\nG50 S6000\r\nG96 S200 M03\r\n...\r\nM9\r\nM05\r\nG97\r\nG54\r\n(T0202 EM)\r\nT0202\r\nG98\r\nM1001\r\nM1003 S3000\r\n```\r\n\r\n### The rule, and why (full entry: `docs/decisions/1173-g97-before-live-tool.md`)\r\n\r\n**The section end cancels G96 when the section posted it.** I picked this over \"every section start states its own mode\" because every following section goes through the section end, whatever its kind: live tool, drill on centre, thread, tap, probe, speed 0, no spindle stated, a legacy stream, or a kind added later. A rule at the start would have to be repeated in every `startPreamble` branch. It also could not cover the program boundary: the header states no spindle mode, so an unconditional `G97` in the live branch would change every live-tool program, including ones that never had a G96. The section-end rule changes only programs that post a G96.\r\n\r\nThe cost: one bare `G97` line per CSS section. Two CSS sections in a row post `G96 S200 M03` ... `M05` / `G97` / ... `G96 S200 M03` ... `M05` / `G97`. The flip is harmless because the spindle is already stopped, and it is pinned as the negative case.\r\n\r\nUnchanged: when G96 is chosen, the G50 / `D` clamp logic (machine, tool and workholding limits), the per-rev feed words, and every program with no G96 section.\r\n\r\nTormach PathPilot lathe has no live branch: it does not declare `liveTooling`, so the engine refuses a C section by name. Its drill and thread sections could still follow a G96 section, so it gets the same rule.\r\n\r\n## Goldens that changed\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc`: one line gained:\r\n  ```\r\n   M9\r\n   M05\r\n  +G97\r\n   G28 U0 W0\r\n   M30\r\n  ```\r\n  No other existing golden changed. Every lathe golden (`lathe_post`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread`, `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_unwind`, `conformance`, `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`) and every recorded per-post golden is byte-identical, because none of them posts a G96.\r\n- New: recorded case `css_then_live` (stream `crates/post/tests/recorded/streams/css_then_live.cnc`, built and guarded by `recorded_streams.rs`). It posts on a test-bench fixture `crates/post/tests/recorded/machines/millturn-live.mch`: the shipped `millturn.mch` plus placeholder live-tool words M1001-M1004. These are not a real builder's codes, so the file stays a test fixture and is not shipped. `recorded::machine_of` now returns a path so a case can use such a fixture. `fanuc-lathe/css_then_live.nc` shows `M05` / `G97` before the live branch. Every other post refuses the C section by name: 10 new `.refusal` goldens.\r\n- Assertions updated because of the new `G97`: `lathe_post_css::applying_the_turning_suggestion...` (it said \"no G97 at all\"; now: no `G97 S`, one bare `G97` after `M05`) and `lathe_post_tormach::css_arcs_part_load_and_a_trip_home_speak_linuxcnc` (it now ends `M9 M5 G97 G30 M30`).\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n- `lathe_post_refusals::a_live_tool_section_after_a_css_one_posts_g97_before_its_live_spindle`: the twin with a `LiveTool` section. It asserts `M05\\nG97\\nG54\\n(T0202 EM)\\nT0202\\nG98\\nM1001\\nM1003 S3000\\n` and checks that the live section's own end adds nothing.\r\n- `lathe_post_refusals::a_thread_after_a_css_section_opens_under_g97`: `G97` is the mode word before the thread's first S.\r\n- `lathe_post_refusals::a_drill_after_a_css_section_finds_g97_already_in_force`: the same check for a drill on centre.\r\n- `lathe_post_refusals::two_css_sections_in_a_row_each_state_their_own_g96` and `lathe_post_tormach::two_css_sections_in_a_row_each_state_their_own_g96`: the negative case. Exactly two `G96` lines and two bare `G97` lines, no `G97 S`, and the program ends in `G97`.\r\n- `lathe_post_tormach::a_section_without_surface_speed_posts_g97_after_one_with_it`: extended so the CSS section ends `M5\\nG97\\n`.\r\n- `script_*::css_then_live` (all 11 per-post suites) and `recorded_streams::css_then_live_stream_is_current`.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`: every suite green.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` on `lathe_post`, `lathe_post_css`, `lathe_post_tormach`, `lathe_post_tormach_thread`, `lathe_post_refusals`, `lathe_workholding_rpm`, `c_axis_live`, `c_axis_unwind`, `lathe_cycle_exit`, `lathe_spindle_law`, `conformance`, `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`, `recorded_post_streams`: all green.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on the final head: it ran the post suites (all 19 binaries: ok) and, because a shared golden (`facing_css.nc`) changed, every app suite (1195 s). All green except `coarse_laws`: 4 tests, which are already red on main at 6a10c5ad and unrelated to this diff. The test expects the old refusal text \"re-import with a larger budget\", and `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE` on main says \"larger STEP facet budget\". That is tracked by #1175 / #1178. What the gate chose: post: axis_direction_cli, comp, comp_plane, cycle_hop, mch_head_search, post_engine, recorded_streams, script_* (11); app: every suite (shared test input `tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/facing_css.nc`).\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- Not run on a real control. The behaviour of a bare `G97` on a stopped spindle comes from the Fanuc-style and LinuxCNC public programming references, not from a machine.\r\n- The live-tool words in the fixture are placeholders.\r\n- The workholding-clamp interaction was not re-derived: `lathe_workholding_rpm` is green and the clamp code is untouched.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The lathe posts (Fanuc lathe, Tormach PathPilot lathe) cancel constant surface speed with G97 at the end of every section that used G96, so a following live-tool, drilling or threading section never runs its S word as a surface speed (#1173)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nFixes #1173\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
